      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 526194876,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "This looks right.\n\nAccording to RFC 6385, one of the version bits should actually be 'experimental', but I have no idea if it was ever used as such.  Rather than add a new field, would be good to add a value_string (or range_string?) for hf_vp8_hdr_version and add the values from the table, i.e.\n\n            +---------+-------------------------+-------------+\n            | Version | Reconstruction Filter   | Loop Filter |\n            +---------+-------------------------+-------------+\n            | 0       | Bicubic                 | Normal      |\n            |         |                         |             |\n            | 1       | Bilinear                | Simple      |\n            |         |                         |             |\n            | 2       | Bilinear                | None        |\n            |         |                         |             |\n            | 3       | None                    | None        |\n            |         |                         |             |\n            | Other   | Reserved for future use |             |\n            +---------+-------------------------+-------------+",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
